    <span class="part-tag">Part I · 101 First Principles</span>
    <h2>1. Hyperfactoring the Hardware–Runtime Cartesian Product</h2>
    <p>A mainstream CPU flattens a dependency graph into a sequential array of instructions, then spends the majority of its die area and dynamic power trying to reconstruct the parallelism and ownership it just destroyed: instruction fetch/decode, branch predictors, reorder buffers (<code>tomasulo-run-sound</code>), and multi-core <code>MESI</code> snoop directories (<code>mesi-wr-swmr</code> in <code>lib/silicon/arch.hypercubical</code>). Formalizing or designing such a machine confronts the Cartesian product $\mathrm{ISA} \times \mathrm{ROB} \times \mathrm{MESI} \times \mathrm{GC} \times \mathrm{PnR}$.</p>
    <p>In <code>lib/silicon/inet-fabric.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/silicon/hypernet.hypercubical</code>, and <code>lib/silicon/hypernet16.hypercubical</code>, lowering <code>src/net.c</code> and <code>src/dnf.c</code> directly to gates factors that product into orthogonal conservation and commutation laws:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Degree-2 Wire Linearity Kills Cache Coherence (<code>vxchg-order-sym</code>):</strong> Every interaction-net wire has exact degree 2. A wire slot needs only two states (<code>vslot-empty | vslot-wait ep</code>) updated by a 1-cycle atomic exchange: the first arriving endpoint parks its word and immediately reclaims its cell ID; the second swaps the slot back to empty and fires an active redex. Partitioning wire IDs by their low 4 bits across 16 tiles (<code>var-home16</code>, <code>striped-var16-certs</code>) eliminates central switches and L1/L2/L3 cache coherence completely.</li>
      <li><strong>Binary Universal Combinators Kill Variable-Arity Heaps &amp; GC (<code>beta-is-con-annihilate</code>, <code>dup-con-commutes-conserves</code>):</strong> Currying closures and constructors into fixed-width 2-port <code>UCell</code> rows (<code>uc-era | uc-con | uc-dup</code>) turns higher-order $\beta$-reduction (<code>APP</code> meeting <code>LAM</code>) into 1-cycle <code>CON–CON</code> annihilation (2 → 0 cells) and closure sharing into 2 → 4 commutation conserving $\mathrm{live} + |\mathrm{freeStack}|$ on each tile's local LIFO stack.</li>
      <li><strong>§4.5 Cubical Face Restriction Kills Speculative Rollback (<code>hnode-conflict-prunes-subgraph</code>, <code>ucell-conflict-erases</code>):</strong> Instead of speculating down dead branches and rolling back register checkpoints, each redex carries bit-vector interval clauses $(\mathrm{pa}, \mathrm{na}), (\mathrm{pb}, \mathrm{nb})$. A 15-gate combinational meet unit evaluates $\mathrm{conf} = \bigvee((\mathrm{pa} \lor \mathrm{pb}) \land (\mathrm{na} \lor \mathrm{nb}))$ in ~25 ps: when any interval dimension requires $r_k = 0 \land r_k = 1$, the tile annihilates the entire contradicted subgraph at its root in <strong>1 clock cycle</strong>.</li>
    </ul>

