    <h2>3. SkyWater 130nm <code>tt_um_hyperinet</code> v2 &amp; 16-Tile 7nm <code>HyperNet-16</code> Signoff</h2>
    <p>On the physical <strong>SkyWater 130nm</strong> Tiny Tapeout target (<code>lib/silicon/inet-fabric.hypercubical</code>), the single-lane Lafont core synthesizes to <strong>3,826 cells</strong> and <strong>24,529.78 µm²</strong> (2.63× smaller than the von Neumann <code>hypercore_soc</code>), while the programmable <strong>dual-lane superscalar <code>tt_um_hyperinet</code> v2</strong> (firing 2 disjoint redexes per clock edge with fused <code>NUM/ADD/ADD1</code> and runtime external graph loading) synthesizes to <strong>11,247 cells</strong> (211 flip-flops vs. 554 in <code>hypercore_soc</code>, <strong>2.63× fewer FFs</strong>) in <strong>65,738.05 µm²</strong>.</p>
